{"agent_id":"pp3g-w20v-task-rebuild-the-hub-reduced-issues-projection-in-the","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-06T13:58:54.264386102Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1f2b3808-3b73-48b5-9fc6-86719bc50eee","comment_uuid":"335107db-e8eb-4024-a729-16260ccac07e","author":"pp3g-w20v-task-rebuild-the-hub-reduced-issues-projection-in-the","content":"Plan: investigation complete — mapping fork mechanisms (read-only) to determine if a safe v3→projection rebuild exists. FINDINGS SO FAR: (1) v3 checkpoint ref carries the full modern reduced state (state.json = 232 issues, next_display_id=235, no collisions); (2) the v2 worktree projection .hub-cache/issues/ (4 June-era files) is NEVER written by v3 — materialize() (compaction.rs:1006) is only called from the v2 compaction path (compaction.rs:375) which is refused on v3 hubs (compact.rs:54 bail); (3) migrate hub-v3 is v2→v3 direction (build_genesis_from_files migrate_hub_v3.rs:747), not v3→projection, and --finalize refuses on ASES per #142; (4) migrate to-shared on v3 routes to to_shared_v3 (event-log promotion, migrate.rs:213) — no worktree writes; (5) integrity hydration --repair on v3 re-hydrates SQLite from reduced state (integrity_cmd.rs:335) — no worktree writes; (6) the v3 checkpoint's OWN browse tree is also stale (4 files from 2026-06-23) because compact_v3's idempotency guard (hub_v3.rs:1594-1614) + incremental-only browse ops (hub_v3.rs:1616, full=!browse_present) prevent a full rebuild once README.md exists. CONCLUSION: likely NO safe crosslink mechanism regenerates the reduced issues/ projection from v3 refs; per task step 4 I will document the exact manual procedure on #233 instead of forcing anything. Next: verify binary gate (ade6146b) behavior, then write the procedure doc (Research Addendum 04 §2.9) + verdict.","created_at":"2026-08-06T13:58:54.256544643Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:mnzZUiZYbWbkCmYT841sUfzxk6ejYNtO+bzcEp7B4VQ","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgvRL8